add('ofer','ofer','ofer','preference','preposition',{'inflection':'invariant','government':'accusative'},'above; more than, in preference','47.10','U18-EX-P32 U18-CRAWFORD1922-P195','ofer ūs ealle: above us all, in the father’s preference/love. Crawford44.20 directly prints he lufaþ hine ænne ofer us ealle. Keep this comparative preference sense distinct from spatial over and authority.',sid='ofer-u18-preference')
add('for','for','for','cause','preposition',{'inflection':'invariant','government':'dative'},'because of; on account of','45.6','U18-EX-P30 U18-CRAWFORD1922-P191','for ðǣm fēo: on account of that money, the cause of their apprehension. Supply the exact causal frame. It is not for a beneficiary or a substitution.',sid='for-u18-cause')
add('for','for','for','benefit','preposition',{'inflection':'invariant','government':'dative'},'for; to the benefit of','48.6','U18-EX-P33','for ēowerre ðearfe: for your good/benefit. Keep the whole phrase visible with the selected dative singular ðearfe; earlier beneficiary for supports the relation but not every new abstract complement.',sid='for-u18-benefit')
